%N A400649 Indices q at which A327008 decreases: A327008(q+1) = A327008(q) - 1.
%C A400649 Here A327008(q) is the number of iterations of the integer Newton map x -> floor((x + floor(q^2/x))/2), starting with x = q^2, until it reaches x = q.
%C A400649 Values A327008(a(n)) are listed in A400650.
%C A400649 It is conjectured that this sequence is infinite.
%e A400649 A327008(1984) = 14 and A327008(1985) = 13, so a(1) = 1984.
%e A400649 A327008(45904) = 19 and A327008(45905) = 18, so a(2) = 45904.
%Y A400649 Cf. A327008, A400650.
